Package: impactpexa
Title: IMPACT Prognostic Models for Traumatic Brain Injury - ModelsCloud Service
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ramin", "Rezaeianzadeh", email = "raminrzn@student.ubc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ewout W.", "Steyerberg", role = "ctb",
           comment = "First author of the IMPACT prognostic models"),
    person("Andrew I.R.", "Maas", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Senior author of the IMPACT prognostic models"))
Description: Implements the IMPACT prognostic models for traumatic brain
    injury described in Steyerberg et al. (PLoS Medicine 2008)
    <doi:10.1371/journal.pmed.0050165>. Estimates the probability of 6-month
    mortality and 6-month unfavourable outcome in adults with moderate to
    severe TBI (Glasgow Coma Scale 12 or less) from admission characteristics,
    across three nested models of increasing complexity: Core, Core+CT
    (Extended) and Core+CT+Lab. Uses the continuous regression coefficients
    published by the IMPACT investigators, so results match the authors'
    own calculator rather than the rounded score chart in the paper.
